{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
The [Am]only [C]thing a [D]drunkard [F]needs
Is a [Am]suitcase [C]and a [E7]trunk
The [Am]only [C]time that he's [D]half satis[F]fied
Is [Am]when he's [E7]on a [Am]drunk
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Go and [Am]tell my [C]baby [D]sister[F]
[Am]Never do [C]like I have [E7]done
[Am]Shun that [C]house down in [D]New Or[F]leans
That they [Am]call that [E7]Rising [Am]Sun
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
It's [Am]one foot [C]on the [D]plat[F]form
[Am]One foot [C]on the [E7]train
I'm [Am]going [C]back down to [D]New Or[F]leans
To [Am]wear my [E7]ball and my [Am]chain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
My [Am]life is [C]almost [D]o[F]ver
My [Am]race is [C]almost [E7]run
[Am]Going back [C]down to [D]New Or[F]leans
To [Am]that house of the [E7]Rising [Am]Sun
{end_of_verse}

